## Current findings and residual work

The first discovery pass surfaced three real active semantic lifecycle-drift findings in this
workspace: `LOOP-E23AE1BA0FD3` (IDEA-0018), `LOOP-1E2AB8FF492F` (IDEA-0019), and
`LOOP-E1E6B5F7FDEA` (IDEA-0020). They are reported but deliberately not mitigated by this campaign.

Two recovery gaps were observed and are retained for later roadmap work:

1. An absent Hybrid database can be recreated as an invalid empty SQLite file by a read/report or
   post-install path. M2 should remove this side effect and add regression coverage.
2. Losing a local reporter outbox can reset sequence numbers below the hosted instance watermark,
   causing otherwise valid reports to be rejected as stale. M4 should implement bounded reporter
   sequence recovery/convergence rather than requiring manual test-bed repair.

The historical backlog is not declared clean. M2 must add the remaining current outcome and
lineage finding classes; M3 must perform supervised, manifest-bound historical review.

